  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760197,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1942 (MSX) - Synopsis\n\nExperience the thrill of aerial combat in *1942*, a classic vertically scrolling shooter brought to the MSX! Developed by Capcom and released in 1986, this arcade hit transports you to the Pacific Theater of World War II, where you take on the role of a daring \"Super Ace\" fighter pilot. Your mission: to reach Tokyo and dismantle the Japanese air fleet.\n\nInspired by the pivotal Battle of Midway, *1942* offers fast-paced, engaging gameplay. Begin each level from an aircraft carrier and navigate through waves of enemy planes and anti-aircraft fire. Collect power-ups to enhance your firepower and increase your chances of survival. A unique \"loop-the-loop\" maneuver allows you to dodge enemy attacks, adding a layer of skill to the action.\n\nAs the first game in the successful *194X* series, *1942* set the standard for Capcom's vertical shooters. With its accessible gameplay and challenging difficulty, *1942* on MSX provides a nostalgic and exhilarating experience for fans of classic arcade games. Prepare for intense dogfights and a desperate fight for victory!"
    },
